<title>UK: UK's Northern jumps on bid clearance.</title>
<headline>UK's Northern jumps on bid clearance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Northern Electricity Plc jumped on Friday as the UK government cleared the bid from U.S. utility CE Electric.  </p>
<p>Northern shares were up 40p at 642-1/2 by 1117 GMT and shares in other regional electricity companies also rose, with London Electric up 23-1/2p at 675, Southern Electric up 27-1/2 at 775 and Yorkshire Electricity up 16p at 758-1/2.</p>
<p>East Midlands Electricity was up 26p at 652-1/2.  </p>
<p>Trade and Industry Minister Ian Lang said he had cleared the bid after gaining assurances from CE relating to Northern's financial and management resources and on maintaining Northern's financial status.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
